<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia reviews Skase chase decision.</title>
<headline>Australia reviews Skase chase decision.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Prime Minister John Howard said on Thursday the government would review a decision to end funding for efforts to recover assets from failed media tycoon Christopher Skase.</p>
<p>&quot;I have asked the attorney-general to examine whether it is appropriate to overturn a decision of the bankruptcy authorities,&quot; Howard told parliament.</p>
<p>Government authorities had decided to end funding for efforts to recover assets from the bankrupt former Qintex Ltd chief, now living in self-imposed exile in Spain.</p>
</text>
